		"description": "Light bodies on strong, steep but non-breaking deep-water waves. Seven 0.06 kg, 0.15 m radius beach balls (hollow-sphere inertia, ~1.1 cm draft) sit along the main wave direction at different wave phases, and a light 4 x 1.6 x 0.6 m, 400 kg boat floats at y = 8. Both waves use the deep-water dispersion relation (omega = sqrt(g*k)): a 12 m swell with 0.75 m amplitude (ka = 0.39, T = 2.8 s) and a 6 m cross-wave with 0.25 m amplitude (ka = 0.26). The largest combined downward surface acceleration (about 6.4 m/s^2) stays below g, so a real floating body never leaves the surface; any body that jumps clear of the water shows a simulation artefact. Bodies start near their floating draft.",
